course: dictionary
lesson: 10853
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so the sentence tells you which one is meant. «At the vet's, a microchip about the size of a grain of rice slides under the skin.» The clues are vet's, puppy and microchip, so vet means an animal doctor here.
explain: Vet can also be a verb, a doing word. «To vet someone or something means to check them carefully before accepting them.» Look for clues such as to, will or the word before it. Then swap in check carefully and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes the clue is a whole phrase. «Sea lions learn to lie still for vet checks without sleep medicine» means health checks by an animal doctor. Ask yourself: what kind of vet is this? Animal doctor, checker, or ex-soldier? The clues will tell you.
fact: A vet is an animal doctor who looks after sick or injured animals.
fact: Vets treat pets, farm animals and zoo animals, for check-ups, vaccinations and treatment.
fact: In the USA, «vet» is short for veterinarian; in the UK the full name is veterinary surgeon.
fact: As a verb, «vet» means to check someone or something carefully before accepting them.
fact: In the USA, «vet» can also mean a veteran, a person who used to be in the army or navy, as in «a war vet».
exercise: «At the vet's, a microchip about the size of a grain of rice slides under the skin.» What does vet mean here? | A wooden fence | A type of sweet | A person who checks things carefully | *An animal doctor
exercise: Dad says, «The club will vet every new coach before they start.» What does vet mean in this sentence? | To give an injection | To ask a question | To play a game | *To check carefully before accepting
exercise: «Sea lions learn to lie still for vet checks without sleep medicine.» What are vet checks? | *Health checks by an animal doctor | Races between animals | Clean-up days at the zoo | Games for sea lions
test: «Grandpa was a war vet who served in the army.» What does vet mean here? | A type of cat | *A veteran, a person who used to be in the army | An animal doctor | To check carefully
test: «The dog's paw was hurt, so we took it to the vet.» What does vet mean here? | *An animal doctor | A wooden fence | A kind of boat | A person who checks things carefully
exam: Which sentence uses vet as a verb, meaning to check carefully? | The vet's bill came in the post today | Grandad is a war vet from the navy | Our dog had a check-up at the vet | *The club will vet every new coach carefully before they start
